<title>HONG KONG: Yue Yuen yearly profit rises 13.02 pct.</title>
<headline>Yue Yuen yearly profit rises 13.02 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   30.4     vs 29.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    7.0	vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    763.43   vs 675.48</p>
<p>    Turnover		     4,194.95 vs 4,057.78</p>
<p>    Company name		 Yue Yuen Industrial (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  March 20-27</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 7</p>
<p>NOTE -  Yue Yuen is a sports shoe manufacturer.</p>
<p>The company will put to shareholders for approval a proposal to consolidate every five existing shares into one new share and to reduce the board lot for trading from 2,000 shares to 1,000 consolidated shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is 11 H.K. cents (including an interim dividend of four cents) vs 10 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
